# ── never publish: the moat ──
# The film grades are the one input no competitor can reproduce. The arithmetic
# is public (that is the brand's transparency promise); the grades are not.
exports/
# EVERY database file, not just this one name. `data/model.db` alone does not
# match `data/model.pre-v2-20260906T050202Z.db` -- the timestamped backups
# migrate_v2.py writes before it applies. Those are byte-for-byte copies of the
# grade database, they are 20 MB each, and they were sitting untracked and
# unignored one `git add -A` away from the public repository.
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
# The research bundle embeds every film grade. It is deployed to the PRIVATE
# Vercel repo, never to this public one.
site/research/data.json
output/research/
data/cache/
data/api_budget.json

# ── never publish: internal analysis + secrets ──
# FINDINGS.md is marked Internal/working and critiques the model candidly.
# SETUP.md contains real Google Sheet IDs.
# NOTE: a '#' only starts a comment at the START of a line. An inline comment
# becomes part of the pattern and silently matches nothing.
FINDINGS.md
SETUP.md
service-account*.json
*.env

# ── the state journal ──
# It lives on its own `data-state` branch, published by tools/state_commit.sh
# from a REDACTED copy. The working journal here holds the film grades in full
# and must never reach a commit on this branch.
state/
.state-publish/

# ── generated ──
output/
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# Dev-only QA harness dependencies; never shipped to the site.
node_modules/
tools/qa/package-lock.json
